  "note": "Triennial election of the Coleraine Borough Council, 15 May 1936; sixteen nominations for sixteen seats, returned unopposed (Derry Journal, 6 May 1936, p. 8). The report heads the item 'Sixteen nominations for sixteen seats' and ends 'These were returned unopposed.' The Belfast Telegraph of the same date carries the same nominations. No party label was printed. New candidates named: Henry, Sutherland, M'Clean, M'Candless, W. C. Dalzell, Tredennick and M'Donald. Returned unopposed."
